{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:122", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "122", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "When calamity, famine, old age or disease has no remedy, the noble call the giving up of the body for the sake of dharma sallekhanā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["death-dying", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:sallekhana"], "concepts": ["cpt:sallekhana"], "practices": ["prc:sallekhana"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "restricted": true, "notes": "Restricted: the text's own conditions only. Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:136-147", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "136-147", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The householder rises through eleven stages (pratimā): right view, vows, equanimity, fasting on holy days, giving up living food, not eating at night, celibacy, giving up undertakings, giving up possessions, not approving [household acts], and not accepting food prepared for oneself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:pratima"], "concepts": ["cpt:eleven-pratimas"], "practices": ["prc:pratimas"], "paths": ["pth:jain-eleven-pratimas"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:2", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "2", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "I teach the true dharma, which destroys karma and which lifts beings out of the suffering of saṃsāra and holds them in the highest happiness.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:dharma"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:3", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "3", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The lords of dharma know right view, knowledge and conduct as dharma; their opposites are the road of worldly existence.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:ratnatraya", "trm:dharma"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-jewels"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:4", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "4", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Right view is faith in the true deity (āpta), scripture and ascetic teacher, free of the three follies and the eight prides, and possessed of the eight limbs.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:samyag-darsana", "trm:mudhata", "trm:mada"], "concepts": ["cpt:samyaktva"], "obstacles": ["obs:three-mudhatas", "obs:eight-madas"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:43-46", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "43-46", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Right knowledge includes the four expositions (anuyoga): the narratives of great persons, the analysis of the world and karma, the rules of conduct, and the doctrine of substances.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:anuyoga"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-anuyogas"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:5", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "5", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The true deity must be free of faults, omniscient and the teacher of scripture; otherwise there can be no true deity.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:arhat", "trm:sarvajna", "trm:vitaraga"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-marks", "cpt:pancaparamesthin"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:ratnakarandasravakacara:66", "source": "src:ratnakarandasravakacara", "location": {"ref": "66", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The eight basic qualities of the householder are the five small vows together with abstaining from wine, meat and honey.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "terms": ["trm:mulaguna"], "concepts": ["cpt:eight-mulagunas"], "teachers": ["tch:samantabhadra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton). Other authors list the five udumbara fruits instead of the vows.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
